    "type": "question",
    "label": "20",
    "prompt": "First introduce a pronumeral and then solve the equation.\n\nAlice, Betty and Clair share $\\$28$. Betty receives $\\$2$ more than Alice and Clair receives three times as much as Betty. How much does Alice receive?",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "Alice receives $\\$4$.",
      "worked": "Let Alice receive $x$ dollars. Betty receives $x+2$ dollars and Clair receives $3(x+2)$ dollars.\n$$\\begin{align*}x+(x+2)+3(x+2)&=28\\\\x+x+2+3x+6&=28\\\\5x+8&=28\\\\5x&=20\\\\x&=4\\end{align*}$$\nAlice receives $\\$4$.\n\nCheck: Betty receives $\\$6$ and Clair receives $\\$18$. Their total is $4+6+18=28$ dollars.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
